/-!
# The period lattice of uncoupled harmonic oscillators

Consider finitely many uncoupled harmonic oscillators, the `i`-th of mass `m i` and angular
frequency `ν i`, on the phase space `V × V`, `V = EuclideanSpace ℝ ι`, of positions `q` and
momenta `p`, with its standard symplectic form `ω₀ = Σ dqᵢ ∧ dpᵢ`. Their energies are

`Eᵢ(q, p) = pᵢ² / (2 mᵢ) + mᵢ νᵢ² qᵢ² / 2`

(`TauCeti.oscillatorEnergies m ν`), each the energy `TauCeti.oscillatorHamiltonian` of one
oscillator read in the `i`-th phase plane `(qᵢ, pᵢ)`. For nonzero masses and frequencies:

* The energies Poisson-commute, their regular points are the points at which no phase plane
  coordinate pair `(qᵢ, pᵢ)` vanishes, and they form a completely integrable system
  (`TauCeti.isIntegrableSystem_oscillatorEnergies`).
* The Hamiltonian flow of `Eᵢ` rotates the `i`-th phase plane and fixes the others. Together these
  flows give the action of `ℝ^ι` generated by the energies
  (`TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic.hamiltonianFlowAction`), and `v` acts by the linear map
  `TauCeti.oscillatorRotation m ν v`, which turns the `i`-th phase plane through the angle
  `νᵢ vᵢ`:

  `qᵢ ↦ cos (νᵢ vᵢ) qᵢ + sin (νᵢ vᵢ) pᵢ / (mᵢ νᵢ)`,
  `pᵢ ↦ -mᵢ νᵢ sin (νᵢ vᵢ) qᵢ + cos (νᵢ vᵢ) pᵢ`

  (`TauCeti.hamiltonianFlowAction_oscillatorEnergies_apply`).
* At a point at which every `(qᵢ, pᵢ)` is nonzero, the stabilizer of this action, the period
  lattice of the invariant torus through the point, is `⊕ᵢ (2π / νᵢ) ℤ`
  (`TauCeti.hamiltonianFlowStabilizer_oscillatorEnergies`). It does not depend on the torus. For
  positive masses and nonzero frequencies these points are those at which every energy is positive
  (`TauCeti.oscillatorEnergies_pos_iff`).

The actions of the oscillators are `Iᵢ = Eᵢ / νᵢ` (`TauCeti.oscillatorAction`), so the energies are
`f(I) = (νᵢ Iᵢ)ᵢ` as functions of the actions. In the normalization of the Liouville–Arnold
theorem the period lattice is `2π (D_I f)^(-T) ℤ^ι`, the transpose lattice of `2π` times the
derivative of the actions as functions of the energies
(`TauCeti.hamiltonianFlowStabilizer_oscillatorEnergies_eq_transposeLattice`). In the
action–angle coordinates of each oscillator (`TauCeti.oscillatorActionAngle`), the vector `v`
fixes the actions and translates the angles by `νᵢ vᵢ`
(`TauCeti.oscillatorRotation_apply_of_eq_oscillatorActionAngle`), so the energies act on each
invariant torus by translations of the angle torus `(ℝ / 2πℤ)^ι`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.oscillatorEnergies m ν`: the energies of uncoupled oscillators on `V × V`.
* `TauCeti.oscillatorRotation m ν v`: the rotation of the phase planes by the angles `νᵢ vᵢ`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.isRegularPoint_oscillatorEnergies_iff`,
  `TauCeti.isIntegrableSystem_oscillatorEnergies`: the energies form an integrable system, regular
  exactly where no phase plane coordinate pair vanishes.
* `TauCeti.isCompleteVectorField_hamiltonianVectorField_oscillatorEnergies`: their Hamiltonian
  vector fields are complete.
* `TauCeti.hamiltonianFlowAction_oscillatorEnergies_apply`: the Hamiltonian flow action of the
  energies is the rotation of the phase planes.
* `TauCeti.hamiltonianFlowStabilizer_oscillatorEnergies`,
  `TauCeti.hamiltonianFlowStabilizer_oscillatorEnergies_eq_transposeLattice`: the period lattice
  is `⊕ᵢ (2π / νᵢ) ℤ = 2π (D_I f)^(-T) ℤ^ι`.
* `TauCeti.oscillatorRotation_apply_of_eq_oscillatorActionAngle`: in action–angle coordinates the
  action of `v` translates the angles by `νᵢ vᵢ`.

## References

* V. I. Arnold, *Mathematical Methods of Classical Mechanics*, second edition, Graduate Texts in
  Mathematics 60, Springer, 1989, Sections 49 and 50.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Set Real
open scoped Manifold ContDiff InnerProductSpace

namespace TauCeti

variable {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {m ν : ι → ℝ}

local notation "𝕍" => EuclideanSpace ℝ ι

/-! ### The energies -/

/-- The energies `Eᵢ(q, p) = pᵢ² / (2 mᵢ) + mᵢ νᵢ² qᵢ² / 2` of uncoupled harmonic oscillators of
masses `m i` and angular frequencies `ν i` on the phase space `V × V`, `V = EuclideanSpace ℝ ι`:
the energy of the `i`-th oscillator is read in the `i`-th phase plane `(qᵢ, pᵢ)`. -/
def oscillatorEnergies (m ν : ι → ℝ) (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) : ι → ℝ :=
  fun i ↦ oscillatorHamiltonian (m i) (ν i) (x.1 i, x.2 i)

omit [Fintype ι] in
theorem oscillatorEnergies_apply (m ν : ι → ℝ) (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) (i : ι) :
    oscillatorEnergies m ν x i = oscillatorHamiltonian (m i) (ν i) (x.1 i, x.2 i) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The position coordinate `qᵢ` is a continuous linear function on the phase space. -/
private def coordFst (i : ι) : (𝕍 × 𝕍) →L[ℝ] ℝ :=
  (PiLp.proj 2 (fun _ : ι ↦ ℝ) i).comp (ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ 𝕍 𝕍)

/-- The momentum coordinate `pᵢ` is a continuous linear function on the phase space. -/
private def coordSnd (i : ι) : (𝕍 × 𝕍) →L[ℝ] ℝ :=
  (PiLp.proj 2 (fun _ : ι ↦ ℝ) i).comp (ContinuousLinearMap.snd ℝ 𝕍 𝕍)

omit [Fintype ι] in
private theorem coordFst_apply (i : ι) (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) : coordFst i x = x.1 i :=
  (rfl)

omit [Fintype ι] in
private theorem coordSnd_apply (i : ι) (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) : coordSnd i x = x.2 i :=
  (rfl)

/-- The energies of uncoupled oscillators are smooth. -/
theorem contDiff_oscillatorEnergies (m ν : ι → ℝ) : ContDiff ℝ ∞ (oscillatorEnergies m ν) := by
  refine contDiff_pi.2 fun i ↦ ?_
  have hq := (coordFst (ι := ι) i).contDiff (n := ∞)
  have hp := (coordSnd (ι := ι) i).contDiff (n := ∞)
  simp only [funext (coordFst_apply i), funext (coordSnd_apply i)] at hq hp
  simp only [oscillatorEnergies_apply, oscillatorHamiltonian_apply]
  exact ((hp.pow 2).div_const _).add ((contDiff_const.mul (hq.pow 2)).div_const _)

/-- **The partial gradients of the energies.** The energy `Eᵢ` has partial gradients
`∇_q Eᵢ = mᵢ νᵢ² qᵢ eᵢ` and `∇_p Eᵢ = (pᵢ / mᵢ) eᵢ`. -/
theorem hasFDerivAt_oscillatorEnergies_apply [DecidableEq ι] (m ν : ι → ℝ) (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) (i : ι) :
    HasFDerivAt (oscillatorEnergies m ν · i)
      ((innerSL ℝ (EuclideanSpace.single i (m i * ν i ^ 2 * x.1 i))).coprod
        (innerSL ℝ (EuclideanSpace.single i (x.2 i / m i)))) x := by
  have hq := (coordFst (ι := ι) i).hasFDerivAt (x := x)
  have hp := (coordSnd (ι := ι) i).hasFDerivAt (x := x)
  simp only [funext (coordFst_apply i), funext (coordSnd_apply i)] at hq hp
  have h := ((hp.pow 2).mul_const (2 * m i)⁻¹).add
    (((hq.pow 2).const_mul (m i * ν i ^ 2)).mul_const 2⁻¹)
  have hE : (oscillatorEnergies m ν · i) =
      fun y : 𝕍 × 𝕍 ↦ y.2 i ^ 2 * (2 * m i)⁻¹ + m i * ν i ^ 2 * y.1 i ^ 2 * 2⁻¹ := by
    ext y
    simp [oscillatorEnergies_apply, oscillatorHamiltonian_apply, div_eq_mul_inv]
  rw [hE]
  refine h.congr_fderiv (ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun w ↦ ?_)
  simp [EuclideanSpace.inner_single_left, coordFst_apply, coordSnd_apply]
  ring

/-- **Hamilton's equations of uncoupled oscillators.** The Hamiltonian vector field of `Eᵢ` is
`qᵢ' = pᵢ / mᵢ`, `pᵢ' = -mᵢ νᵢ² qᵢ` in the `i`-th phase plane, and zero in the others. -/
theorem stdSymplecticForm_hamiltonianVectorField_oscillatorEnergies [DecidableEq ι] (m ν : ι → ℝ)
    (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) (i : ι) :
    (stdSymplecticForm (V := 𝕍)).hamiltonianVectorField (oscillatorEnergies m ν · i) x =
      (EuclideanSpace.single i (x.2 i / m i), -EuclideanSpace.single i (m i * ν i ^ 2 * x.1 i)) :=
  stdSymplecticForm_hamiltonianVectorField (hasFDerivAt_oscillatorEnergies_apply m ν x i)

/-- **The energies of uncoupled oscillators Poisson-commute.** -/
theorem poissonBracket_oscillatorEnergies_eq_zero (m ν : ι → ℝ) (i j : ι) (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) :
    (stdSymplecticForm (V := 𝕍)).constSmooth.poissonBracket (oscillatorEnergies m ν · i)
      (oscillatorEnergies m ν · j) x = 0 := by
  classical
  rw [SymplecticForm.poissonBracket_constSmooth, stdSymplecticForm_poissonBracket
    (hasFDerivAt_oscillatorEnergies_apply m ν x i) (hasFDerivAt_oscillatorEnergies_apply m ν x j)]
  rcases eq_or_ne i j with rfl | hij
  · simp [EuclideanSpace.inner_single_left]
    ring
  · simp [EuclideanSpace.inner_single_left, hij.symm]

omit [Fintype ι] in
/-- For a positive mass and a nonzero frequency, the energy `Eᵢ` is positive exactly where the
coordinate pair `(qᵢ, pᵢ)` does not vanish. -/
theorem oscillatorEnergies_pos_iff {i : ι} (hm : 0 < m i) (hν : ν i ≠ 0) {x : 𝕍 × 𝕍} :
    0 < oscillatorEnergies m ν x i ↔ (x.1 i, x.2 i) ≠ 0 := by
  rw [oscillatorEnergies_apply, oscillatorHamiltonian_apply, Ne, Prod.mk_eq_zero, not_and_or]
  constructor
  · intro h
    by_contra! h0
    simp [h0.1, h0.2] at h
  · rintro (hq | hp) <;> positivity

/-! ### Regular points and integrability -/

/-- **The regular points of uncoupled oscillators.** For nonzero masses and frequencies, the
differentials of the energies are independent at `x` exactly when no phase plane coordinate pair
`(qᵢ, pᵢ)` of `x` vanishes. -/
theorem isRegularPoint_oscillatorEnergies_iff (hm : ∀ i, m i ≠ 0) (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≠ 0)
    {x : 𝕍 × 𝕍} :
    IsRegularPoint 𝓘(ℝ, 𝕍 × 𝕍) 𝓘(ℝ, ι → ℝ) (oscillatorEnergies m ν) x ↔
      ∀ i, (x.1 i, x.2 i) ≠ 0 := by
  classical
  have hF : HasFDerivAt (oscillatorEnergies m ν)
      (ContinuousLinearMap.pi fun i ↦
        (innerSL ℝ (EuclideanSpace.single i (m i * ν i ^ 2 * x.1 i))).coprod
          (innerSL ℝ (EuclideanSpace.single i (x.2 i / m i)))) x :=
    hasFDerivAt_pi.2 fun i ↦ hasFDerivAt_oscillatorEnergies_apply m ν x i
  -- The `i`-th component of the differential is `(δq, δp) ↦ mᵢ νᵢ² qᵢ δqᵢ + pᵢ δpᵢ / mᵢ`.
  have hd (w : 𝕍 × 𝕍) (i : ι) :
      fderiv ℝ (oscillatorEnergies m ν) x w i =
        m i * ν i ^ 2 * x.1 i * w.1 i + x.2 i / m i * w.2 i := by
    simp [hF.fderiv, EuclideanSpace.inner_single_left]
  rw [isRegularPoint_iff_surjective_fderiv]
  constructor
  · intro hs i hi
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hs (Pi.single i 1)
    have h1 := congrFun hw i
    rw [hd] at h1
    simp only [Prod.mk_eq_zero] at hi
    simp [hi.1, hi.2] at h1
  · intro hx c
    -- The sum `Dᵢ = (mᵢ νᵢ qᵢ)² + pᵢ²` is positive, and `δ = (cᵢ mᵢ / Dᵢ) (qᵢ, pᵢ)` is a preimage.
    have hD (i : ι) : m i ^ 2 * ν i ^ 2 * x.1 i ^ 2 + x.2 i ^ 2 ≠ 0 := by
      intro h0
      have h2 : x.2 i = 0 := by nlinarith [sq_nonneg (x.2 i), sq_nonneg (m i * ν i * x.1 i)]
      have h1 : m i * ν i * x.1 i = 0 := by
        nlinarith [sq_nonneg (x.2 i), sq_nonneg (m i * ν i * x.1 i)]
      have h1' : x.1 i = 0 := by simpa [hm i, hν i] using h1
      exact hx i (by simp [h1', h2])
    refine ⟨(WithLp.toLp 2 fun i ↦ c i * m i / (m i ^ 2 * ν i ^ 2 * x.1 i ^ 2 + x.2 i ^ 2) * x.1 i,
      WithLp.toLp 2 fun i ↦ c i * m i / (m i ^ 2 * ν i ^ 2 * x.1 i ^ 2 + x.2 i ^ 2) * x.2 i), ?_⟩
    funext i
    rw [hd]
    field_simp [hm i, hD i]

/-- **Uncoupled harmonic oscillators form a completely integrable system.** For nonzero masses
and frequencies, the energies `Eᵢ` of uncoupled oscillators are a completely integrable system on
the standard symplectic phase space `V × V`. -/
theorem isIntegrableSystem_oscillatorEnergies (hm : ∀ i, m i ≠ 0) (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≠ 0) :
    (stdSymplecticForm (V := 𝕍)).constSmooth.IsIntegrableSystem (oscillatorEnergies m ν) where
  contMDiff := (contDiff_oscillatorEnergies m ν).contMDiff
  poissonBracket_eq_zero := poissonBracket_oscillatorEnergies_eq_zero m ν
  dense_setOf_isRegularPoint := by
    -- The points at which every momentum coordinate `pᵢ` is nonzero are dense, and regular.
    have hp := (dense_pi univ fun _ _ ↦ dense_compl_singleton (0 : ℝ)).preimage
      (EuclideanSpace.equiv ι ℝ).toHomeomorph.isOpenMap
    refine (hp.preimage isOpenMap_snd).mono fun x hx ↦
      (isRegularPoint_oscillatorEnergies_iff hm hν).2 fun i h ↦ ?_
    simp only [mem_preimage, mem_univ_pi, mem_compl_iff, mem_singleton_iff] at hx
    simp only [Prod.mk_eq_zero] at h
    exact hx i h.2
  two_mul_card_eq_finrank := by
    rw [Module.finrank_prod, finrank_euclideanSpace]
    ring

/-! ### The rotation of the phase planes -/

/-- The **rotation of the phase planes** of uncoupled oscillators by the angles `νᵢ vᵢ`:

`qᵢ ↦ cos (νᵢ vᵢ) qᵢ + sin (νᵢ vᵢ) pᵢ / (mᵢ νᵢ)`,  `pᵢ ↦ -mᵢ νᵢ sin (νᵢ vᵢ) qᵢ + cos (νᵢ vᵢ) pᵢ`.

For nonzero masses and frequencies it is the action of `v` by the Hamiltonian flows of the
energies (`TauCeti.hamiltonianFlowAction_oscillatorEnergies_apply`). -/
def oscillatorRotation (m ν v : ι → ℝ) : (𝕍 × 𝕍) →L[ℝ] 𝕍 × 𝕍 :=
  LinearMap.toContinuousLinearMap
    { toFun x :=
        (WithLp.toLp 2 fun i ↦ cos (ν i * v i) * x.1 i + sin (ν i * v i) / (m i * ν i) * x.2 i,
          WithLp.toLp 2 fun i ↦ -(m i * ν i * sin (ν i * v i) * x.1 i) + cos (ν i * v i) * x.2 i)
      map_add' x y := by ext i <;> simp <;> ring
      map_smul' a x := by ext i <;> simp <;> ring }

@[simp]
theorem oscillatorRotation_apply_fst (m ν v : ι → ℝ) (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) (i : ι) :
    (oscillatorRotation m ν v x).1 i =
      cos (ν i * v i) * x.1 i + sin (ν i * v i) / (m i * ν i) * x.2 i :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem oscillatorRotation_apply_snd (m ν v : ι → ℝ) (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) (i : ι) :
    (oscillatorRotation m ν v x).2 i =
      -(m i * ν i * sin (ν i * v i) * x.1 i) + cos (ν i * v i) * x.2 i :=
  (rfl)

/-- The rotation by the zero vector is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem oscillatorRotation_zero (m ν : ι → ℝ) :
    oscillatorRotation m ν 0 = ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ (𝕍 × 𝕍) := by
  refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun x ↦ ?_
  ext i <;> simp

/-- For nonzero masses and frequencies, the rotation by `v + w` is the rotation by `v` after the
rotation by `w`. -/
theorem oscillatorRotation_add (hm : ∀ i, m i ≠ 0) (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≠ 0) (v w : ι → ℝ) :
    oscillatorRotation m ν (v + w) =
      (oscillatorRotation m ν v).comp (oscillatorRotation m ν w) := by
  refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun x ↦ ?_
  ext i <;>
  · simp only [oscillatorRotation_apply_fst, oscillatorRotation_apply_snd, Pi.add_apply,
      ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, mul_add, cos_add, sin_add]
    field_simp [hm i, hν i]
    ring

/-- For nonzero masses and frequencies, the rotation by `v` is inverted by the rotation by
`-v`. -/
theorem oscillatorRotation_neg_apply (hm : ∀ i, m i ≠ 0) (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≠ 0) (v : ι → ℝ)
    (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) : oscillatorRotation m ν (-v) (oscillatorRotation m ν v x) = x := by
  rw [← ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, ← oscillatorRotation_add hm hν, neg_add_cancel,
    oscillatorRotation_zero, ContinuousLinearMap.id_apply]

/-! ### The Hamiltonian flows of the energies -/

section Flow

variable [DecidableEq ι]

/-- Along the `i`-th coordinate axis the rotation of the phase planes is
`x + (cos (νᵢ t) - 1) (qᵢ, pᵢ) eᵢ + sin (νᵢ t) (pᵢ / (mᵢ νᵢ), -mᵢ νᵢ qᵢ) eᵢ`. -/
private theorem oscillatorRotation_single_apply (i : ι) (t : ℝ) (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) :
    oscillatorRotation m ν (Pi.single i t) x =
      x + (cos (ν i * t) - 1) • (EuclideanSpace.single i (x.1 i), EuclideanSpace.single i (x.2 i)) +
        sin (ν i * t) • (EuclideanSpace.single i (x.2 i / (m i * ν i)),
          EuclideanSpace.single i (-(m i * ν i * x.1 i))) := by
  ext j <;> rcases eq_or_ne j i with rfl | hj <;> simp [*] <;> ring

/-- **The rotation along an axis solves Hamilton's equations.** For nonzero masses and
frequencies, `t ↦ oscillatorRotation m ν (t eᵢ) x` is an integral curve of the Hamiltonian vector
field of the energy `Eᵢ`. -/
theorem hasDerivAt_oscillatorRotation_single {i : ι} (hm : m i ≠ 0) (hν : ν i ≠ 0)
    (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) (t : ℝ) :
    HasDerivAt (fun s ↦ oscillatorRotation m ν (Pi.single i s) x)
      ((stdSymplecticForm (V := 𝕍)).hamiltonianVectorField (oscillatorEnergies m ν · i)
        (oscillatorRotation m ν (Pi.single i t) x)) t := by
  have hθ : HasDerivAt (fun s ↦ ν i * s) (ν i) t := by
    simpa using (hasDerivAt_id t).const_mul (ν i)
  have h := (((hθ.cos.sub_const 1).smul_const
    (EuclideanSpace.single i (x.1 i), EuclideanSpace.single i (x.2 i))).const_add x).add
      (hθ.sin.smul_const (EuclideanSpace.single i (x.2 i / (m i * ν i)),
        EuclideanSpace.single i (-(m i * ν i * x.1 i))))
  refine (h.congr_deriv ?_).congr_of_eventuallyEq (Filter.Eventually.of_forall fun s ↦ ?_)
  swap
  · rw [Pi.add_apply]
    exact oscillatorRotation_single_apply i s x
  rw [stdSymplecticForm_hamiltonianVectorField_oscillatorEnergies]
  ext j <;> rcases eq_or_ne j i with rfl | hj <;> simp [*]
  · field_simp
  · field_simp
    ring

/-- The rotations along the `i`-th axis are global integral curves of the Hamiltonian vector field
of `Eᵢ` for the constant symplectic form on `V × V`. -/
private theorem isMIntegralCurve_oscillatorRotation_single {i : ι} (hm : m i ≠ 0)
    (hν : ν i ≠ 0) (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) :
    IsMIntegralCurve (fun s ↦ oscillatorRotation m ν (Pi.single i s) x)
      ((stdSymplecticForm (V := 𝕍)).constSmooth.hamiltonianVectorField
        (oscillatorEnergies m ν · i)) := fun t ↦ by
  rw [SymplecticForm.hamiltonianVectorField_constSmooth]
  have h := hasDerivAt_oscillatorRotation_single hm hν x t
  rw [hasDerivAt_iff_hasFDerivAt] at h
  exact h.hasMFDerivAt

end Flow

/-- **The Hamiltonian flows of uncoupled oscillators are complete.** For nonzero masses and
frequencies, every integral curve of the Hamiltonian vector field of `Eᵢ` is defined for all time:
it is a rotation of the `i`-th phase plane. -/
theorem isCompleteVectorField_hamiltonianVectorField_oscillatorEnergies {i : ι} (hm : m i ≠ 0)
    (hν : ν i ≠ 0) :
    IsCompleteVectorField
      ((stdSymplecticForm (V := 𝕍)).constSmooth.hamiltonianVectorField
        (oscillatorEnergies m ν · i)) := by
  classical
  refine isCompleteVectorField_of_forall_exists_isMIntegralCurve fun x ↦
    ⟨_, ?_, isMIntegralCurve_oscillatorRotation_single hm hν x⟩
  simp

/-- The rotations of the phase planes, as a homomorphism to the group of diffeomorphisms of the
phase space. -/
private def oscillatorRotationHom (hm : ∀ i, m i ≠ 0) (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≠ 0) :
    (ι → ℝ) →+ Additive ((𝕍 × 𝕍) ≃ₘ^∞⟮𝓘(ℝ, 𝕍 × 𝕍), 𝓘(ℝ, 𝕍 × 𝕍)⟯ (𝕍 × 𝕍)) where
  toFun v := Additive.ofMul
    (ContinuousLinearEquiv.equivOfInverse (oscillatorRotation m ν v) (oscillatorRotation m ν (-v))
      (oscillatorRotation_neg_apply hm hν v)
      fun x ↦ by simpa using oscillatorRotation_neg_apply hm hν (-v) x).toDiffeomorph
  map_zero' := Additive.toMul.injective <| Diffeomorph.ext fun x ↦ by simp
  map_add' v w := Additive.toMul.injective <| Diffeomorph.ext fun x ↦ by
    simp [oscillatorRotation_add hm hν]

/-- **The Hamiltonian flow action of uncoupled oscillators.** For nonzero masses and frequencies,
the vector `v` acts on the phase space through the flows of the energies by rotating the `i`-th
phase plane through the angle `νᵢ vᵢ`. -/
theorem hamiltonianFlowAction_oscillatorEnergies_apply (hm : ∀ i, m i ≠ 0) (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≠ 0)
    (v : ι → ℝ) (x : 𝕍 × 𝕍) :
    ((SymplecticForm.isSymplectic_constSmooth stdSymplecticForm).hamiltonianFlowAction
        (contDiff_oscillatorEnergies m ν).contMDiff (poissonBracket_oscillatorEnergies_eq_zero m ν)
        (fun i ↦ isCompleteVectorField_hamiltonianVectorField_oscillatorEnergies (hm i) (hν i))
        v).toMul x =
      oscillatorRotation m ν v x := by
  classical
  have hσ := SymplecticForm.isSymplectic_constSmooth (stdSymplecticForm (V := 𝕍))
  have hv (i : ι) := hσ.isNondegenerate.contMDiff_hamiltonianVectorField (n := ∞) le_rfl
    (((contDiff_pi.1 (contDiff_oscillatorEnergies m ν)) i).contMDiff (n := ∞ + 1))
  rw [← hσ.eq_hamiltonianFlowAction _ _ _ (oscillatorRotationHom hm hν) hv fun i t ↦ ?_]
  · simp [oscillatorRotationHom]
  · refine Additive.toMul.injective <| Diffeomorph.ext fun y ↦ ?_
    simp only [oscillatorRotationHom, AddMonoidHom.coe_mk, ZeroHom.coe_mk, toMul_ofMul,
      ContinuousLinearEquiv.coe_toDiffeomorph, ContinuousLinearEquiv.equivOfInverse_apply,
      toMul_globalFlowDiffeomorphHom, globalFlowDiffeomorph_apply]
    have h := globalFlow_eq_of_isMIntegralCurve (hv i |>.of_le (by simp))
      (isCompleteVectorField_hamiltonianVectorField_oscillatorEnergies (hm i) (hν i))
      (isMIntegralCurve_oscillatorRotation_single (hm i) (hν i) y) t
    simpa using h.symm

/-! ### The period lattice -/

/-- In a phase plane, the rotation `(q, p) ↦ (c q + s p / a, -a s q + c p)` with `s² + c² = 1`
fixes a nonzero point only when `c = 1`. -/
private theorem cos_eq_one_of_rotation_eq_self {a c s q p : ℝ} (ha : a ≠ 0)
    (hcs : s ^ 2 + c ^ 2 = 1) (hqp : (q, p) ≠ 0) (h₁ : c * q + s / a * p = q)
    (h₂ : -(a * s * q) + c * p = p) : c = 1 := by
  -- Both `q` and `p` are annihilated by `(c - 1)² + s² = 2 - 2c`.
  have hq : (2 - 2 * c) * q = 0 := by
    have : ((c - 1) ^ 2 + s ^ 2) * q = (c - 1) * (c * q + s / a * p - q) -
        s / a * (-(a * s * q) + c * p - p) := by
      field_simp
      ring
    rw [h₁, h₂, sub_self, sub_self, mul_zero, mul_zero, sub_zero] at this
    linear_combination this - q * hcs
  have hp : (2 - 2 * c) * p = 0 := by
    have : ((c - 1) ^ 2 + s ^ 2) * p = a * s * (c * q + s / a * p - q) +
        (c - 1) * (-(a * s * q) + c * p - p) := by
      field_simp
      ring
    rw [h₁, h₂, sub_self, sub_self, mul_zero, mul_zero, add_zero] at this
    linear_combination this - p * hcs
  by_contra hc
  have h2c : 2 - 2 * c ≠ 0 := fun h ↦ hc (by linarith)
  exact hqp (by simp [(mul_eq_zero.1 hq).resolve_left h2c, (mul_eq_zero.1 hp).resolve_left h2c])

/-- **The rotations fixing a point.** For nonzero masses and frequencies, the rotation by `v`
fixes a point `x` at which no phase plane coordinate pair `(qᵢ, pᵢ)` vanishes exactly when every
angle `νᵢ vᵢ` is an integer multiple of `2π`. -/
theorem oscillatorRotation_apply_eq_self_iff (hm : ∀ i, m i ≠ 0) (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≠ 0) {x : 𝕍 × 𝕍}
    (hx : ∀ i, (x.1 i, x.2 i) ≠ 0) {v : ι → ℝ} :
    oscillatorRotation m ν v x = x ↔ ∀ i, ∃ n : ℤ, n * (2 * π) = ν i * v i := by
  refine ⟨fun h i ↦ (cos_eq_one_iff _).1 ?_, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact cos_eq_one_of_rotation_eq_self (mul_ne_zero (hm i) (hν i)) (sin_sq_add_cos_sq _) (hx i)
      (by simpa using congrArg (fun y : 𝕍 × 𝕍 ↦ y.1 i) h)
      (by simpa [mul_assoc] using congrArg (fun y : 𝕍 × 𝕍 ↦ y.2 i) h)
  · have hc (i : ι) : cos (ν i * v i) = 1 := (cos_eq_one_iff _).2 (h i)
    have hs (i : ι) : sin (ν i * v i) = 0 := sin_eq_zero_iff_cos_eq.2 (Or.inl (hc i))
    ext i <;> simp [hc, hs]

/-- **The period lattice of uncoupled harmonic oscillators.** For nonzero masses and frequencies,
at a point at which no phase plane coordinate pair `(qᵢ, pᵢ)` vanishes (for positive masses and
frequencies, a point at which every energy is positive), the stabilizer of the Hamiltonian flow
action of the energies is the lattice `⊕ᵢ (2π / νᵢ) ℤ`. -/
theorem hamiltonianFlowStabilizer_oscillatorEnergies (hm : ∀ i, m i ≠ 0) (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≠ 0)
    {x : 𝕍 × 𝕍} (hx : ∀ i, (x.1 i, x.2 i) ≠ 0) :
    (SymplecticForm.isSymplectic_constSmooth stdSymplecticForm).hamiltonianFlowStabilizer
        (contDiff_oscillatorEnergies m ν).contMDiff (poissonBracket_oscillatorEnergies_eq_zero m ν)
        (fun i ↦ isCompleteVectorField_hamiltonianVectorField_oscillatorEnergies (hm i) (hν i)) x =
      AddSubgroup.pi univ fun i ↦ AddSubgroup.zmultiples (2 * π / ν i) := by
  ext v
  rw [SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic.mem_hamiltonianFlowStabilizer,
    hamiltonianFlowAction_oscillatorEnergies_apply hm hν,
    oscillatorRotation_apply_eq_self_iff hm hν hx]
  simp only [AddSubgroup.mem_pi, mem_univ, true_imp_iff, AddSubgroup.mem_zmultiples_iff,
    zsmul_eq_mul]
  refine forall_congr' fun i ↦ exists_congr fun n ↦ ?_
  rw [mul_div_assoc', div_eq_iff (hν i), mul_comm (v i)]

/-- **The period lattice in action normalization.** The actions of uncoupled oscillators are
`Iᵢ = Eᵢ / νᵢ`. For nonzero masses and frequencies, at a point at which no phase plane coordinate
pair vanishes, the period lattice is the transpose lattice of `2π` times the derivative of the
actions as functions of the energies: `2π (D_I f)^(-T) ℤ^ι` for the energies `f(I) = (νᵢ Iᵢ)ᵢ`. -/
theorem hamiltonianFlowStabilizer_oscillatorEnergies_eq_transposeLattice (hm : ∀ i, m i ≠ 0)
    (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≠ 0) {x : 𝕍 × 𝕍} (hx : ∀ i, (x.1 i, x.2 i) ≠ 0) :
    (SymplecticForm.isSymplectic_constSmooth stdSymplecticForm).hamiltonianFlowStabilizer
        (contDiff_oscillatorEnergies m ν).contMDiff (poissonBracket_oscillatorEnergies_eq_zero m ν)
        (fun i ↦ isCompleteVectorField_hamiltonianVectorField_oscillatorEnergies (hm i) (hν i)) x =
      ((2 * π) • fderiv ℝ (fun c : ι → ℝ ↦ fun i ↦ c i / ν i)
        (oscillatorEnergies m ν x)).transposeLattice := by
  classical
  -- The actions are the diagonal linear map `c ↦ (cᵢ / νᵢ)ᵢ` of the energies.
  have hA : HasFDerivAt (fun c : ι → ℝ ↦ fun i ↦ c i / ν i)
      (ContinuousLinearMap.pi fun i ↦
        (ν i)⁻¹ • ContinuousLinearMap.proj (R := ℝ) (φ := fun _ : ι ↦ ℝ) i)
      (oscillatorEnergies m ν x) := by
    refine hasFDerivAt_pi.2 fun i ↦ ?_
    simpa [div_eq_mul_inv, mul_comm] using
      ((ContinuousLinearMap.proj (R := ℝ) (φ := fun _ : ι ↦ ℝ) i).hasFDerivAt.const_mul (ν i)⁻¹)
  rw [hamiltonianFlowStabilizer_oscillatorEnergies hm hν hx, hA.fderiv]
  ext v
  simp only [AddSubgroup.mem_pi, mem_univ, true_imp_iff, AddSubgroup.mem_zmultiples_iff,
    zsmul_eq_mul, ContinuousLinearMap.mem_transposeLattice, FunLike.coe_smul,
    ContinuousLinearMap.pi_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.proj_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
  constructor
  · intro h
    choose n hn using h
    refine ⟨n, fun w ↦ ?_⟩
    simp only [dotProduct, ← hn]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ by ring
  · rintro ⟨n, hn⟩ i
    refine ⟨n i, ?_⟩
    have h := hn (Pi.single i 1)
    simp only [dotProduct, Pi.single_apply, mul_ite, mul_one, mul_zero, Finset.sum_ite_eq',
      Finset.mem_univ, ↓reduceIte] at h
    rw [h]
    ring

/-! ### Action–angle coordinates -/

/-- **The flows of uncoupled oscillators translate the angles.** If the `i`-th phase plane of `x`
has action–angle coordinates `(θ, I)` for a mass and a frequency with positive product, then that
of its rotation by `v` has action–angle coordinates `(θ + νᵢ vᵢ, I)`. -/
theorem oscillatorRotation_apply_of_eq_oscillatorActionAngle {i : ι} (hmν : 0 < m i * ν i)
    {x : 𝕍 × 𝕍} {θ I : ℝ} (hx : (x.1 i, x.2 i) = oscillatorActionAngle (m i) (ν i) (θ, I))
    (v : ι → ℝ) :
    ((oscillatorRotation m ν v x).1 i, (oscillatorRotation m ν v x).2 i) =
      oscillatorActionAngle (m i) (ν i) (θ + ν i * v i, I) := by
  rw [oscillatorActionAngle_apply] at hx
  obtain ⟨hq, hp⟩ := Prod.mk.inj hx
  rw [oscillatorRotation_apply_fst, oscillatorRotation_apply_snd, hq, hp,
    oscillatorActionAngle_apply, sin_add, cos_add]
  -- Write `B = √(mᵢ νᵢ)`, so that `mᵢ νᵢ = B²`.
  have hB0 : √(m i * ν i) ≠ 0 := (sqrt_pos.2 hmν).ne'
  have hB : m i * ν i = √(m i * ν i) ^ 2 := (sq_sqrt hmν.le).symm
  generalize √(m i * ν i) = B at hB0 hB ⊢
  rw [hB, Prod.mk.injEq]
  constructor
  · field_simp
  · field_simp
    ring

end TauCeti
